| Tier | Name | Risk | What it covers | Reversible |
|------|------|------|----------------|------------|
| Tier 1 | Safe Bloat | Low | Carrier junk, ad daemons, telemetry | Yes |
| Tier 2 | Advanced Debloat | Medium | Secondary assistants, OEM cloud sync | Yes |
| Tier 3 | Extreme Debloat | High | Replaceable stock apps (keyboards, dialers) | Yes |
| Tier 4 | Critical Core | Blocked | Core system packages — never touched | N/A |

## Tier 4: Critical Core Blacklist

Tier 4 packages are permanently hard-blocked under **any** flag or prompt:

- RuleSet.load seeds the critical set from HARDCRITICAL_PACKAGES (89 packages) unioned with critical-do-not-touch.json (61 packages) = **89 unique inviolable packages**.
- Critical packages cannot be disabled or uninstalled under any flag.
- validate_rules.py enforces zero collisions between other rule databases and critical-do-not-touch.json.

Examples of blocked packages: SystemUI, Phone, Settings, and core Android framework components.

## User 0 Preservation

All mutations target user 0 only:

- \`pm disable-user --user 0 <pkg>\` — freeze
- \`pm uninstall -k --user 0 <pkg>\` — uninstall keeping app data via \`-k\`
- \`pm enable --user 0 <pkg>\` — re-enable
- \`cmd package install-existing --user 0 <pkg>\` — restore uninstalled app

This preserves Knox 0x0 warranty status and app private directories.

## Validation

Run the rule validation suite to confirm tier integrity:

\`\`\`bash
python cli/tests/validate_rules.py
\`\`\`

